    <briefdescription>
<para>At-the-money swaption-volatility matrix. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class provides the at-the-money volatility for a given swaption by interpolating a volatility matrix whose elements are the market volatilities of a set of swaption with given option date and swapLength.</para><para>The volatility matrix <computeroutput>M</computeroutput> must be defined so that:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the number of rows equals the number of option dates;</para></listitem><listitem><para>the number of columns equals the number of swap tenors;</para></listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>M[i][j]</computeroutput> contains the volatility corresponding to the <computeroutput>i</computeroutput>-th option and <computeroutput>j</computeroutput>-th tenor. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
